{
  "$comment": [
    "Variant slug -> canonical route. Every entry is served as a permanent redirect.",
    "",
    "JSON rather than TypeScript for one reason: next.config.js is a CommonJS .js file",
    "and cannot import a .ts module, so a TypeScript source would have had to be",
    "duplicated by hand into the config — which is the exact failure this repository",
    "spends most of its guards preventing. Both sides read this file instead:",
    "next.config.js require()s it to build the redirect table, and",
    "content/search/topic-map.ts imports it as ROUTE_ALIASES.",
    "",
    "WHY THESE ARE REDIRECTS AND NOT PAGES: see the header of topic-map.ts. The short",
    "version is that thirty-odd near-identical pages are a doorway set under Google's",
    "published spam policy, they split the link equity and crawl budget one page would",
    "concentrate, and an answer engine deduplicates them into a single weak citation",
    "target before it ranks anything.",
    "",
    "Adding an entry: the destination must be a route that exists. verify-topic-map.mjs",
    "fails the build if it does not, and fails if a key collides with a real route."
  ],
